> Typically, home users have been subjected to very few, true performance NAS products. If you wanted true performance, you had to reach a little deeper into your pocket, and pull out a bit more of that hard earned money.
With Netgear being an industry leader in network storage solutions, it seems only fitting that they would offer top to bottom[ storage] solutions for every sector of the market. Today, on this crisp winter morning, we will be looking over the Netgear ReadyNAS 104. The[ RN]104 is[ a four bay NAS] appliance[ that] caters[ to] the needs of consumers that want personal cloud[ storage].[ It offers standard] features like a home media and file[ server], coupled together[ with] low entry cost[.]
The RN[104] is built upon the Marvell ARMADA 370 platform, clocked at 1.2 GHz, with 512MB of memory to accompany it[.] Across the front of the unit, we[ have four] 3.5[" drive] tr[ays that support] tool-[less installation. Total storage capacity] is listed at[ 16]TB[, with] dual gigabit LAN[ ports] at the[ rear of] the unit[.]
For quick management of the NAS, we[ have] a two[ line LCD] screen on the front[ of] the unit,[ with] dual[ USB 3].[0 ports], and e[SATA] for[ additional storage] options[.] Power consumption is listed at 45 watts for operation, and 1.4 watts with WOL enabled.
Pricing of the[ four] bay Netgear ReadyNAS 104 is listed at $319.99, without drives. The unit carries a three-year warranty from Netgear.

